Package: srividhya
Type: Package
Title: SRIvidhya: Site-Adaptive Alternate Wetting and Drying Decision Support Tools for Rice
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Rakesh", "Tiwari", email = "shimogarakesh@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Implements a proposed site-adaptive alternate wetting and drying (AWD)
    decision-support and monitoring, reporting, and verification (MRV) framework for
    irrigated rice, as described in Tiwari et al. (commentary manuscript, submitted).
    SRIvidhya replaces a single universal AWD water-table depth with transparent,
    locally calibrated functions covering variety-specific root development, profile
    representative water-table decline, root-safe drainage ceilings, dual depth/tension
    drainage verification, and soil-organic-carbon-scaled drainage-event frequency.
    SRIvidhya is a decision-support tool. It is not a universal methane emission-factor
    model, not an autonomous carbon-credit calculator, and not a replacement for direct
    greenhouse-gas measurement where such measurement is feasible. All scientifically
    sensitive parameters (maximum rooting depth, root growth-rate parameters, percolation
    rate, root-safety margin, drainage-depth ceiling, soil-water-potential threshold, and
    soil-organic-carbon frequency anchors) must be supplied by the user with an explicit
    evidence tier; the package does not hard-code universal defaults for these values.
